  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nA cold front will move across the area today. Latest guidance trends\nsuggest that any convective development along/ahead of the boundary\nwill most likely be east of the region. However, there could be some\nspotty post-frontal showers.\n\nHigh pressure will build in for Friday and Saturday. There will still\nbe a diurnal cumulus field Friday but few clouds on Saturday.\nTemperatures will only warm slightly, getting close to normal\nSaturday.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nA pattern shift will occur over the weekend into early next week.\nTroughing over eastern North America will dampen allowing a mid level\nhigh over the southwest US to expand and move eastward. The high will\nbecome centered over the Tennessee Valley by Tuesday. This will\nresult in increasing temperatures and dew points as well as dry\nconditions. Heading into midweek, there is a bit of uncertainty\nwhether a back door cold front could get into the region and bring\nthe next chance of showers and storms.",
